title: A Crisis Compact
subtitle: A hostile cabinet may still need votes for a narrow material response.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_negotiation_card
view-if: left_in_government = 0 and government_has_confidence = 1 and caretaker_government = 0 and month_actions < max_month_actions and poland_crisis_compact_timer <= 0 and national_crisis_pressure >= 25
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_crisis_compact_timer = 4
card-image: img/poland/deck_social.svg

= A crisis compact from opposition

**Government:** [+ government_name +], led by [+ prime_minister +].  
**Lewica's role:** [+ left_role +].

The cabinet does not become friendly because the country is under pressure.
It may, however, exchange a bounded concession for votes, implementation
capacity and shared responsibility.

Current leverage: **[+ negotiation_leverage +]/100**. Crisis pressure:
**[+ national_crisis_pressure +]/100**. Government hostility:
**[+ government_negotiation_hostility +]/100**.

[? if government_party = "pis": PiS demands **54** for a deal. The score is
the visible leverage above plus the option bonus; there is no hidden roll.?]
[? if government_party != "pis": The current cabinet demands **44**. The score
is the visible leverage above plus the option bonus; there is no hidden roll.?]

- @targeted
- @maximal
- @walk

@targeted
title: Offer votes for a ninety-day wage, energy and care shield
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource · score +10 · success at 54 under PiS, 44 otherwise.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: A costed amendment and monitoring team require one resource.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.negotiation_attempts += 1;
Q.negotiation_last_score = Math.round(
    (Number(Q.negotiation_leverage) || 0) + 10
);
Q.negotiation_last_threshold =
    Q.government_party == "pis" ? 54 : 44;
Q.negotiation_last_result =
    Q.negotiation_last_score >= Q.negotiation_last_threshold
        ? "Targeted crisis compact accepted"
        : "Targeted crisis compact refused";
Q.negotiation_success =
    Q.negotiation_last_score >= Q.negotiation_last_threshold ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.negotiation_success) {
    Q.negotiation_successes += 1;
    Q.negotiation_capital += 3;
    Q.household_security += 5;
    Q.health_capacity += 2;
    Q.government_delivery += 3;
    Q.public_service_families_left_affinity += 3;
    Q.industrial_logistics_left_affinity += 3;
    Q.provincial_welfare_left_affinity += 2;
    Q.pis_relation += Q.government_party == "pis" ? 3 : 0;
    Q.ko_relation += Q.government_party == "ko" ? 3 : 0;
    Q.public_trust += 2;
    Q.news_headline =
        "A costed opposition compact wins a narrow government concession";
} else {
    Q.negotiation_capital -= 2;
    Q.public_trust -= 1;
    Q.pis_cohabitation_rally +=
        Q.government_party == "pis" ? 3 : 0;
    Q.news_headline =
        "The government refuses the crisis compact and claims the offer was theatre";
}
!}
go-to: result

@maximal
title: Demand the whole Left emergency programme
subtitle: Cost: 2 resources · score +16 · threshold rises by 12 for the larger package.
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The full package requires two resources of drafting and coalition work.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 2;
Q.negotiation_attempts += 1;
Q.negotiation_last_score = Math.round(
    (Number(Q.negotiation_leverage) || 0) + 16
);
Q.negotiation_last_threshold =
    (Q.government_party == "pis" ? 54 : 44) + 12;
Q.negotiation_last_result =
    Q.negotiation_last_score >= Q.negotiation_last_threshold
        ? "Full emergency programme accepted"
        : "Full emergency programme refused";
Q.negotiation_success =
    Q.negotiation_last_score >= Q.negotiation_last_threshold ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.negotiation_success) {
    Q.negotiation_successes += 1;
    Q.negotiation_capital += 5;
    Q.household_security += 8;
    Q.health_capacity += 4;
    Q.labor_credibility += 5;
    Q.government_delivery += 5;
    Q.public_service_families_left_affinity += 4;
    Q.industrial_logistics_left_affinity += 4;
    Q.provincial_welfare_left_affinity += 3;
    Q.party_unity += 2;
    Q.fiscal_stress += 4;
    Q.news_headline =
        "Crisis pressure forces the cabinet to accept a broad Left package";
} else {
    Q.negotiation_capital -= 3;
    Q.party_unity += 1;
    Q.public_trust -= 2;
    Q.pis_cohabitation_rally +=
        Q.government_party == "pis" ? 5 : 0;
    Q.news_headline =
        "The maximal package unites the Left and gives the cabinet an easy refusal";
}
!}
go-to: result

@walk
title: Refuse shared responsibility and publish the government's refusal price
subtitle: No deal test · opposition clarity +3 unity · crisis delivery does not improve.
on-arrival: negotiation_success = 0; negotiation_last_result = "No compact attempted"; negotiation_last_score = negotiation_leverage; negotiation_last_threshold = 54 if government_party = "pis"; negotiation_last_threshold = 44 if government_party != "pis"; party_unity += 3; media_capacity += 2; government_delivery -= 1; public_trust -= 1; pis_relation -= 2; ko_relation -= 1; news_headline = "Lewica leaves the crisis response entirely to the cabinet"
go-to: result

@result
title: The crisis offer
new-page: true

= A visible bargaining result

**[+ negotiation_last_result +]**  
Score **[+ negotiation_last_score +]** · required **[+
negotiation_last_threshold +]**.

[? if negotiation_success: The agreement is narrow, published and
implementable. Lewica remains outside government; it has bought policy, not a
ministry or a share of the state budget.?]

[? if not negotiation_success and negotiation_last_result != "No compact attempted":
The cabinet keeps control of the response and gains a short confrontation.
Lewica keeps its votes and pays for a failed approach.?]

[? if negotiation_last_result = "No compact attempted": No causal ambiguity
remains: cabinet delivery and failure now belong to the government alone.?]

- #poland_card_finish
